    "rfi.intro_title": "Get a clear answer on the record",
    "rfi.intro_body": "Raise a question to the design team, set who owns the next move and a response due date, then track it from Open to Answered to Closed with a ball-in-court badge and an overdue counter. Attach the drawings in question from Documents, and when an answer carries cost you can spin it straight into a Variation. Export the full RFI log for the contract file.",
    "rfi.intro_more": "Press **New RFI** and write the subject and question, set a priority, pick a discipline, name who holds the ball in court and an assignee, then add a response due date. You can attach the drawings in question, either ticking existing project documents or dropping a file straight into the dropzone to upload it. Each RFI opens from Open to Answered to Closed, and the row shows a ball-in-court badge plus a running days-open and overdue counter.\n\nWhen an answer carries cost, expand an answered or closed RFI and press **Create Variation** to push it into the commercial trail. Attachments are pulled from Documents, the ball-in-court person comes from your team, and answered RFIs feed Correspondence as a linked thread.\n\n**Getting the most out of it:**\n- Use the saved-view chips (Mine, Awaiting me, Overdue) to scan what is on your plate.\n- Set a realistic due date so the overdue pill flags stalls early.\n- Flag cost impact on the RFI so the Variation hand-off is one click later.",
    "submittals.col_pipeline_sr": "Pipeline",
    "submittals.days_in_court": "{{days}}d in court",
    "submittals.days_in_court_sla_breach": ", SLA breached",
    "submittals.due_in": "Due in {{days}}d",
    "submittals.due_overdue": "Overdue {{days}}d",
    "submittals.due_today": "Due today",
    "submittals.pipeline_approved": "Approved",
    "submittals.pipeline_approved_noted": "Approved as Noted",
    "submittals.pipeline_aria": "Submittal status pipeline",
    "submittals.pipeline_closed": "Closed",
    "submittals.pipeline_draft": "Draft",
    "submittals.pipeline_rejected": "Rejected",
    "submittals.pipeline_revise": "Revise & Resubmit",
    "submittals.pipeline_submitted": "Submitted",
    "submittals.pipeline_under_review": "Under Review",
    "submittals.intro_title": "No work installed without sign-off",
    "submittals.intro_body": "Log each shop drawing, product data sheet, sample or certificate and move it through Draft, Submitted, Under Review, then Approved or Revise-and-resubmit, with a due-date and days-in-court badge so nothing stalls. Link a submittal to the BOQ positions it covers so you can see which items have approved documentation before they go to site.",
    "submittals.intro_more": "Press **New Submittal**, give it a title and spec section, pick the type (shop drawing, product data, sample, mock-up, test report, certificate or warranty) and a date required. The submittal starts as Draft, then you Submit it for review. A reviewer opens it and records a decision: Approved, Approved as Noted, Revise and Resubmit, or Rejected, with comments. A Revise-and-resubmit sends it back so the submitter edits and resubmits as the next revision.\n\nThe row carries a days-in-court badge and a due-date countdown so nothing stalls. Where your project has a submittal approval route configured under Governance, a multi-step sign-off runs instead of the direct review. Submittals can link to the BOQ positions they cover, and supporting files live in Documents.\n\n**Getting the most out of it:**\n- Link each submittal to its BOQ positions so you can see what has approved documentation before it goes to site.\n- Watch the days-in-court badge to chase a slow reviewer.",
