    "procurement.invoice_requires_issue": "Issue the purchase order before invoicing",
    "dwg_takeoff.import_doc_failed": "Could not open this document in DWG Takeoff",
    "dwg_takeoff.opening_document": "Opening document…",
    "dwg_takeoff.opening_document_hint": "Preparing this drawing for takeoff. This can take a few minutes for large DWG files.",
    "dwg_takeoff.intro_title": "Measure straight off the 2D drawing",
    "dwg_takeoff.intro_body": "Upload DWG or DXF drawings to view their entities, toggle layers, and measure areas, lengths and counts directly on the plan. Link measurements to BOQ positions so the quantities flow into your cost estimate alongside BIM and the canonical model.",
    "dwg_takeoff.intro_more": "Upload a DWG or DXF drawing and it renders as 2D entities on a canvas. Toggle layers in the right panel to clear the clutter, then pick a measurement tool from the toolbar to measure distances, areas and counts directly on the plan. Calibrate the scale first if the drawing units are unknown, so measurements come out in real metres. Each measurement you keep can be linked to a BOQ position, and you can compare two revisions of a drawing side by side in the compare drawer.\n\nThis is the 2D CAD counterpart to the BIM viewer: it handles the .dwg and .dxf files that the BIM Hub turns away. Measurements linked here flow into the BOQ alongside quantities from BIM models and PDF takeoff, so a job that mixes 2D drawings and 3D models still rolls up into one estimate. You can also export the marked-up canvas to PDF.\n\n**Getting the most out of it:**\n- Calibrate the scale before measuring anything, an uncalibrated drawing produces meaningless lengths.\n- Turn off layers you are not measuring so snapping lands on the right line.\n- Use the revision compare to re-measure only what changed instead of redoing the whole sheet.",
    "dwg_takeoff.intro_link_boq": "Open BOQ",
    "dwg_takeoff.intro_link_bim": "BIM viewer",
    "takeoff.landing_drop_here": "Drop a PDF here or click to browse",
    "takeoff.landing_drop_pdf_only_title": "PDF only",
    "takeoff.landing_dropzone_aria": "Drop a PDF here or click to browse.",
    "takeoff.landing_dropzone_hint": "Architectural drawings · floor plans · sections · scans",
    "takeoff.landing_feat_ai_desc": "Let the AI extract walls, slabs and rooms from a drawing, you review and confirm before committing.",
    "takeoff.landing_feat_ai_title": "AI-assisted quantities",
    "takeoff.landing_feat_click_desc": "Distance, area, polyline and count tools, click directly on the PDF to capture quantities.",
    "takeoff.landing_feat_click_title": "Click-to-measure",
    "takeoff.landing_feat_export_desc": "Send measurements straight into your Bill of Quantities, with links back to the source drawing.",
    "takeoff.landing_feat_export_title": "Export to BOQ",
    "takeoff.landing_feat_scale_desc": "Two-point calibration or preset scales (1:50, 1:100), every measurement stays accurate.",
    "takeoff.landing_feat_scale_title": "Scale calibration",
    "takeoff.landing_feat_units_desc": "Switch freely between m, m², m³, pcs, grouped by trade with hide/show per layer.",
    "takeoff.landing_feat_units_title": "Area · length · count",
    "takeoff.landing_fmt_primary": "Primary",
    "takeoff.landing_hero_subtitle": "Click-to-measure on any drawing, lengths, areas, counts, with AI that suggests quantities and sends them straight into your BOQ.",
    "takeoff.landing_hero_title": "PDF Takeoff",
    "takeoff.landing_supported_formats": "Supported formats",
    "takeoff.landing_what_you_get": "What you get",
    "takeoff.intro_title": "Measure straight off the drawing",
    "takeoff.intro_body": "Upload PDF drawings to measure areas, lengths and counts by hand, or let AI extract elements with quantities. Selected measurements flow straight into your BOQ and stay linked to the project cost and schedule.",
    "takeoff.intro_more": "Upload a PDF drawing and measure right on it. Open a document and use the on-screen tools to measure areas, lengths and counts by hand, or let the AI analysis extract elements with quantities and a confidence score for each. Extracted elements list by category with totals, and you choose which ones to keep. There is also a compare drawer to set two drawing revisions against each other.\n\nHow measurements travel:\n\n- Selected measurements and accepted elements flow into your **BOQ** as positions with quantities.\n- They stay linked to the project, so the quantities tie back to project cost and schedule, and you can switch between this and the other routes on the **Quantities** page.\n\n**Getting the most out of it:** Review the AI confidence on each element before accepting it, since low-confidence items deserve a manual check against the drawing. Use the compare drawer when a new revision lands so you re-measure only what changed. Confirm the unit on each measurement so it lands in the BOQ as the quantity you expect.",
