    "finance.link_to_5d": "5D Cost Model",
    "finance.no_evm_no_budget_desc": "EVM is computed from your project budget and paid invoices. Add budget lines first, then create a snapshot to track schedule and cost performance.",
    "finance.project_currency": "project currency",
    "finance.tabs_aria": "Finance sections",
    "finance.view_5d_model": "Open 5D Cost Model",
    "finance.intro_title": "See where the money actually went",
    "finance.intro_body": "Set budget lines against your WBS, then track invoices and payments as they land so committed, actual and forecast sit next to the original budget with the variance called out. The earned value dashboard turns that into cost and schedule performance, and budgets can pull straight from the BOQ estimate and 5D cost model.",
    "finance.intro_more": "Finance is organized in five tabs: Budgets, Invoices, Payments, EVM Dashboard and Connectors. Start on Budgets by adding budget lines against your WBS categories, or import them from Excel. Each line tracks original, revised, committed, actual and forecast side by side, with the variance colored green when under budget and red when over. Log invoices as payable or receivable, record payments against them, and watch the summary cards and the budget-consumption bar update. The EVM Dashboard turns it into cost and schedule performance once a project has cost data.\n\nFinance pulls from and pushes to the cost side of the platform:\n\n- Lock a **BOQ** estimate and click Create Budget from Estimate to seed your budget lines automatically.\n- The **5D Cost Model** and Finance share the same budget and actuals so the numbers stay aligned.\n- Purchase orders raised in **Procurement** flow in as committed spend, and invoices roll up into Actual once paid.\n\n**Getting the most out of it:**\n\n- Seed budgets from a locked BOQ instead of typing them, it keeps the WBS and the estimate in step.\n- Every record carries its own currency; when a project spans several, set FX rates so totals convert cleanly rather than reading as approximate.\n- Watch the budget-consumed bar, it flags over 80 percent as watch and over 95 percent as critical.",
